  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ali P.M vs State Of Kerala on 27 November, 2025 2025:Ker:91606 Crl.M.C.No.4297 & 2890 of 2020 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice G.Girish Thursday, The 27Th Day Of November 2025 / 6Th Agrahayana, 1947 Crl.Mc No. 4297 Of 2020 Crime No.428/2020 Of Kothamangalam Police Station, Ernakulam Against The Order/Judgment Dated In Cc No.220 Of 2020 Of Judicial First Class Magistrate Court - Ii, Kothamangalam Petitioner/S: 1 Gulfam Ansari Aged 33 Years S/O. Mohammed Ummar Ansari, H/S. 177, Nagarnigam, Saharanpur, Jain Colony, Uttar Pradesh, Now Residing At Kottarathil Koyon'S Buildings, Companypady, Nellikuzhy, Ernakulam District 2 Asif Aged 33 Years S/O. Mohammed Sakeer, Farman Basthi, Gadgeri, Saharnpur, Jain Colony, Uttar Pradesh, Now Residing At Kottarathil Koyon'S Buildings, Companpady,Nellikuzhy, Ernakulam District. 3 Shiyas, Aged 34 Years S/O. Mohammed, Kottarathil House, Schoolpady, Eramalloor Village, Nellikuzhy, Ernakulam District. By Advs. Sri.Deepak Raj Smt.C.P.Roopa Ali P.M vs State Of Kerala on 27 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55814238/ 1 Respondent/S: 2025:Ker:91606 Crl.M.C.No.4297 & 2890 of 2020 2 State Of Kerala Represented By The Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam-682 031 Other Present: Sri Renjit George, Sr Pp,Smt Seena C, Pp This Criminal Misc. Case Having Come Up For Admission On 27.11.2025, Along With Crl.MC.2890/2020, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: 2025:Ker:91606 Crl.M.C.No.4297 & 2890 of 2020 3 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice G.Girish Thursday, The 27Th Day Of November 2025 / 6Th Agrahayana, 1947 Crl.Mc No. 2890 Of 2020 Crime No.428/2020 Of Kothamangalam Police Station, Ernakulam Petitioner/Accused Nos.2 To 4: Ali P.M Aged 44 Years S/O. Makkar, Padinjarechalil House, Iramalloor Village, Poomattam Kavala, Kothamangalam Taluk, Ernakulam District-Pin-No.686691. By Advs. Sri.P.K.Varghese Shri.T.M.Sudheer Ali P.M vs State Of Kerala on 27 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55814238/ 2 Respondent/Complainant: 1 State Of Kerala Represented By The Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam-682031. 2 Ranjini Ravi, W/O. Ravi, Ottuman House, Iramalloor Village, Nellikuzhy, Kothamangalam Taluk, Ernakulam District-Pin-686691. This Criminal Misc. Case Having Come Up For Admission On 27.11.2025, Along With Crl.MC.4297/2020, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: 2025:Ker:91606 Crl.M.C.No.4297 & 2890 of 2020 4 Order",
    "facts": "2. The prosecution case is that on 30.03.2020, the petitioners made propaganda through Facebook, making use of the cell phone of the first petitioner, that the community kitchen being maintained by Nellikuzhi Grama Panchayath under the presidentship of the defacto complainant, has been serving sub standard food, and collecting huge amount from the public for the same. According to the prosecution, the aforesaid propaganda made during COVID period, was intended to give provocation to cause riot. The allegation against the petitioners is that they made publication through Facebook, criticising the food being distributed through the community kitchen of Nellikuzhi Grama Panchayat, by making the following posts.",
    "arguments": "For charging a person with the commission of offence under Section 118(e) of the Kerala Police Act, 2011, there should be sufficient materials to show that such person knowingly did any act, which caused danger to the public,or failure in public safety. The offence under Section 120(o) of the Kerala Police Act will be attracted, if it is shown that a person, by way of any means of communication, caused nuisance of himself to any other person by repeated or undesirable or anonymous call, letter, writing, message, e-mail or through a messenger.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "For charging a person with the commission of offence under Section 118(e) of the Kerala Police Act, 2011, there should be sufficient materials to show that such person knowingly did any act, which caused danger to the public,or failure in public safety. The offence under Section 120(o) of the Kerala Police Act will be attracted, if it is shown that a person, by way of any means of communication, caused nuisance of himself to any other person by repeated or undesirable or anonymous call, letter, writing, message, e-mail or through a messenger."
  },
